# The pause menu, which no recorded case reaches past opening it: a hole played to two putts, then
# the menu opened and each of its screens visited in turn — Volume (a page over the hole), the
# Score card, Help (a menu of its own) — and then Resume, back to the hole with the strokes kept.
#
# Checked against the pure recompilation (tests/vs-recomp.sh), not against a recording. The wheel
# has to wait for the menu to settle: turning it while the hole is still placing the ball resumes
# the game instead, which is why this pauses after the second putt rather than at the start.
200: select
300: wheel +240
400: wheel +240
500: wheel +24
800: select
1100: select
1500: select
2000: select
2500: select
3000: select
3600: shot
3700: select
4200: shot
4300: select
4700: wheel +16
5000: shot
5100: select
5400: select
6000: shot
6300: select
7000: shot
7200: select
7600: wheel -8
7900: select
8200: select
9000: shot
9200: menu
9800: wheel +8
10200: select
10900: shot
11100: menu
11900: shot
12100: wheel +8
12500: select
13200: shot
13400: menu
14200: shot
14400: wheel +8
14800: select
15500: shot
15700: menu
16500: shot
16700: wheel -32
17100: select
17900: shot
18000: quit
